       No errors are defined in X/Open Curses.  This implementation checks for
       null  pointers,  returns EERRRR in that case.  Also, the _m_v routines check
       for error moving the cursor, returning EERRRR  in  that  case.   Otherwise
       they return OOKK.

       Functions  prefixed with “mv” first perform cursor movement and fail if
       the position (_y, _x) is outside the window boundaries.

